The Makefile.PL in the working directory is untracked (.gitignore) and hand-written: it resolves flags via pkg-config. The Makefile.PL that dzil generates (see Net-LibSSH-0.002/Makefile.PL) goes through Alien::libssh->cflags/->libs. A perl Makefile.PL && make && make test cycle therefore links against a different libssh than the release does, and a green local run says nothing about the released build. The old CLAUDE.md documented that local cycle as the build instruction. Decide: delete the stray file, or keep it and document it as a dev-only shortcut.
